# Mission plan

**Execution model:** Squad Leader inventories GitHub vulnerability alerts with **`gh`**, triages recommended fixes with the developer, applies (or plans) lockfile/code patches using each scoped repo’s documented procedures (app/ucsf **`backend/README.md`** / **`frontend/README.md`** vulnerability sections; **infra** npm / Terraform / Helm; **ml-flows** **uv** locks), then reuses plan-and-deliver **`new-plan`** / **`pr-plan`** / **`coding-session`** to ship changes in **that scoped GitHub repo** when code changes are required. **Forbidden:** inventing patch procedures that contradict those READMEs; treating hosting **`HOSTING_ROOT`** / `safebeat-sedea/sedea-app` as the remediation tree; Squad Leader proposing dispatch resolution without documenting residual open alerts in scope; opening a vulnerability PR before a same-scope **`gh`** re-inventory confirms no missed in-scope alerts (or residuals are explicitly deferred); opening a vulnerability PR before required product-repo tests pass (or an explicit same-turn waiver).

**Skill reuse:** [`.sedea/centers/software-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/`](.sedea/centers/software-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/) — **`new-plan`**, **`pr-plan`**, **`coding-session`**, **`pr-review`**. Spawn contracts: [`.sedea/centers/software-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/README.md`](.sedea/centers/software-development/missions/plan-and-deliver/skills/README.md). Low-complexity single-PR patches may follow [quick-fix](.sedea/centers/software-development/missions/quick-fix/plan.mdc) constraints (complexity ≤6) when the developer confirms.

## Mission constraints (binding)

| Constraint | Rule |
|------------|------|
| **Inventory source** | Prefer **`gh`** (`gh api` / Dependabot / code-scanning / advisory surfaces available to the authenticated user) over manual guesswork |
| **Patch procedures** | **App/ucsf:** Backend Poetry patches per each product repo’s `backend/README.md` § *Vulnerability patches of transitive dependency directly in poetry.lock*; frontend Yarn patches per `frontend/README.md` § *Vulnerability version patches directly in yarn.lock* — under the scoped **`safebeat/app`** or **`safebeat/ucsf-study`** tree, **not** hosting-repo `app/` paths. **Infra / ml-flows:** Follow §5 *Extended ecosystem patch appendix* — do not substitute app README steps for uv/npm/Terraform/Helm alerts. |
| **Target repositories** | Vulnerability inventory and remediation may target GitHub repos **`safebeat/app`**, **`safebeat/ucsf-study`**, **`safebeat/infra`**, and **`safebeat/ml-flows`**. **Forbidden:** treating the Sedea hosting repo (`safebeat-sedea/sedea-app` or this workspace’s **`HOSTING_ROOT`**) as an inventory or remediation target (edits land on the **scoped remote repo** via worktree/clone — not anonymous paths under hosting main). Within app/ucsf, resolve backend/frontend (Poetry/Yarn) from **that** repo’s layout. **`safebeat/ml-flows`** is **not** a hosting submodule — use a dedicated clone/worktree on **`safebeat/ml-flows`**. **`safebeat/infra`** may be edited via the **`infra/`** submodule remote when checked out. Narrow to one repo (and optional severity/package filter) via §3 scope pick or a clear opening remainder — **do not** inventory all repos by default when the developer has not chosen. |
| **Host shell** | Mission Control Shell has **no Python** — run Poetry/Yarn via documented host tooling or interactive terminal presets when credentials/interactive auth are required; do not invent `python3` workflows |
| **Ship chain** | Product lockfile/code changes ship via detached **`coding-session`** (same order as plan-and-deliver §8) — do not duplicate ship-chain steps here |
| **Vulnerability PR metadata** | When §8–§9 open a product-repo PR for this mission: **`--title`** must be `Vulnerabilities Fix - (YYYY-MM-DD)` (UTC calendar day of `gh pr create`). **`--body`** must be a markdown list of applied fixes as `package from -> to` (e.g. `aiohttp 5.1.2 -> 5.1.6`); optional one-line summary above the list. **Forbidden:** appending a “Made with Cursor” (or equivalent IDE) tag/footer; inventing titles that omit the date suffix. This mission binding **supersedes** generic `create-pr` past-tense title guidance for these PRs only. |
| **Pre-PR re-check** | After fixes are applied and **before** `gh pr create`, re-run the same-scoped **`gh`** inventory (§6). **Forbidden:** opening the vulnerability PR while in-scope alerts remain open unless the developer explicitly deferred them this turn. |
| **Pre-PR tests** | After §6 `proceed-to-pr` (or explicit residual deferral) and **before** `gh pr create`, run required product-repo tests for ecosystems touched by `applySet` (§7). **Forbidden:** opening the PR while required tests fail unless the developer explicitly waives in structured choice this turn. |
| **Out of scope** | Rewriting Sedea center governance; closing GitHub alerts without verifying the fix; force-ignoring alerts without documented deferral |

